        "status": "draft",
        "page": "spin-geometry-dirac-and-index-theory",
        "axiom_strength": "ZF + full AC; inherited from compact elliptic and spectral suppliers",
        "statement": "Assume full AC. For a closed even-dimensional manifold and a graded Hermitian geometric Clifford module, let $P=D_V^2$ with the $H^2$ selfadjoint domain. Its spectrum is discrete, nonnegative, of finite multiplicities, and has smooth eigensections. For $t>0$, $e^{-tP}$ is trace class and has a smooth kernel $K_t(x,y)$. The diagonal series and its derivatives converge uniformly for each $t>0$, and\n$$\\operatorname{ind}_{\\mathbb C}D_V^+=\\operatorname{Str}(e^{-tP})=\\int_M\\operatorname{str}K_t(x,x)\\,d\\operatorname{vol}_g(x),\\qquad t>0.$$"
      },
