        "page": "spin-geometry-dirac-and-index-theory",
        "axiom_strength": "ZF + full AC",
        "statement": "Assume the full Axiom of Choice. Let $E\\to M$ be an oriented Euclidean smooth real vector bundle of rank $n\\ge1$ over a Hausdorff second-countable smooth manifold. Then $E$ admits a Spin lift of [[def-spin-lift-of-oriented-orthonormal-frame-bundle]] if and only if $w_2(E)=0\\in H^2(M;\\mathbb F_2)$. When nonempty, isomorphism classes of lifts form a torsor under $H^1(M;\\mathbb F_2)$: twisting a lift by a principal $\\{\\pm1\\}$-bundle gives a free and transitive action. No distinguished lift is asserted. Rank zero is excluded."
      },
