        "page": "spin-geometry-dirac-and-index-theory",
        "axiom_strength": "ZF + full AC; exact current Clifford/Spin interfaces",
        "statement": "Assume full AC and the hypotheses of [[lem-getzler-radial-gauge-oscillator-leading-term]]. In the finite-dimensional even exterior-form algebra at $y$, the heat equation for $P_0$ has the normalized Gaussian solution\n$$k_t(x,0)=(4\\pi t)^{-m}\\det^{1/2}\\!\\left(\\frac{t\\mathcal R/2}{\\sinh(t\\mathcal R/2)}\\right)\\exp\\!\\left(-\\frac{1}{4t}x^T\\bigl((t\\mathcal R/2)\\coth(t\\mathcal R/2)\\bigr)x\\right)e^{-tF^{V/S}}.$$\nThe square root is the formal branch with constant term $1$. Its degree-$2m$ diagonal supertrace coefficient, interpreted as an oriented top form using [[def-riemannian-volume-form-on-an-oriented-manifold]] and the curvature convention of [[def-ahat-and-relative-chern-character-forms]], is exactly $[\\widehat A(TM,\\nabla^{LC})\\operatorname{ch}(V/S)]_{2m}$."
